*======================================================================
* modstub.a99 - the first 96 bytes of a module program's file
* (tools/skmodprog.py puts it there; docs/MODPROG.md).  The file is an
* Editor/Assembler option 5 image for >2000, so a machine that has no kernel
* cartridge to run it with (the Editor/Assembler's own option 5, say) calls
* this: it says what the program needs and returns.  The kernel cartridge's
* RUN PROGRAM FILE never runs it: it recognises the signature after the stub.
*======================================================================
       AORG >2000
STUB   LIMI 0
* the VDP write address of row 11, column 1: >4000 + 11 x 32 + 1
       LI   R0,>4161
       SWPB R0
       MOVB R0,@>8C02
       SWPB R0
       MOVB R0,@>8C02
       LI   R1,MSG
       LI   R2,MSGE-MSG
SL     MOVB *R1+,@>8C00
       DEC  R2
       JNE  SL
       RT
MSG    TEXT 'NEEDS THE SAMS KERNEL CARTRIDGE'
MSGE
